      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(tui): suppress unhandled rejection from editor submit handlers",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`createEditorSubmitHandler` calls `params.handleBangLine`, `params.handleCommand`, and `params.sendMessage` as fire-and-forget `void` expressions. Because those params are typed `Promise<void> | void`, an async rejection would become an unhandled rejection and could crash the TUI process.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdded a small `suppressHandlerRejection` helper that only attaches a `.catch` when the handler actually returns a promise. When it rejects, a generic stderr diagnostic is written and the error is swallowed, matching the existing agent-session abort fallback pattern.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThe TUI is more resilient to rare async failures in command/message handlers; users see a brief diagnostic instead of a process crash.\n\n## Evidence\n\nTerminal proof (after fix):\n\n```bash\nnode_modules/.bin/tsx scripts/proof/tui-submit-rejection-catch.mts\n```\n\nOutput:\n\n```\n=== Proof: tui-submit rejecting handler catch ===\n\nTriggering bang-line, command, and send-message handlers that all reject...\n\nAll rejecting handlers were caught; no unhandled rejections.\n\nPASS: tui-submit suppresses async handler rejections.\n```\n\nRegression test:\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/tui/tui-submit.test.ts\n```\n\nAll 4 tests pass.\n",
        "branch": "fix/tui-submit-rejection-catch",
        "head_sha": "04e1ed3cc73c1c034148fa0904bfe75bc27eada2",
